<style>
#form-ID-container {
	container-type: inline-size;
}
#form-ID {
	grid-template-areas:
		'section-header-1'
		'enable'
		'keep'
		'maxAgeDays'
		'section-header-2'
		'keepImages'
		'keepFiles'
		'trash'
		'maxFileSizeMB';
	grid-template-columns: 1fr;
}
@container (min-width: 500px) {
	#form-ID {
		grid-template-areas:
			'section-header-1  .'
			'enable .'
			'keep maxAgeDays'
			'section-header-2  .'
			'keepImages keepFiles'
			'trash maxFileSizeMB';
		grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
	}
}
</style><div id="form-ID-container"><form id="form-ID" class="totalform help-on-hover help-box formgrid" data-method="POST" data-api="/api" data-route="/admin/settings/backups"><h3 class="form-grid-section-header" style="grid-area: section-header-1;" data-section-fields="enable keep maxAgeDays">Object History</h3><h3 class="form-grid-section-header" style="grid-area: section-header-2;" data-section-fields="keepImages keepFiles trash maxFileSizeMB">Uploaded Files</h3><div class="form-field toggle-field " data-type="toggle" style="--grid-area: enable;"><label for="field-UID">Keep Object History</label><div class="form-group"><div class="switch"><input id="field-UID" name="enable" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="help-UID" checked/><label for="field-UID" aria-hidden="true">Keep Object History</label></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Master switch. When off, saves and deletes write no snapshots and no files are kept. Existing snapshots are left in place and still restore. Sync's pre-overwrite snapshots are unaffected by this setting.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: keep;"><label for="field-UID">Snapshots per Object</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="keep" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="10" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="10" min="1" max="100" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">The newest snapshots each object keeps; older ones are pruned on the next save. Identical consecutive saves do not stack a duplicate. Raise this on a busy editorial site; it only costs the size of the record's JSON per snapshot.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: maxAgeDays;"><label for="field-UID">Maximum Age (days)</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="maxAgeDays" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="30" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="30" min="0" max="3650" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Applies to snapshots and to uploaded files: a snapshot, a kept image or file, or anything in the trash is deleted once it is older than this, whatever the counts say. Without it, one busy afternoon of edits would evict last week's version, the one you actually wanted. Set to <code>0</code> to switch the age rule off: snapshots and kept images and files then stay until their count removes them, and the trash is emptied after 30 days.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: keepImages;"><label for="field-UID">Earlier Images per Field</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="keepImages" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="0" min="0" max="50" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">How many replaced or removed images each <code>image</code> field of an object keeps, so restoring a snapshot brings its image back. That includes an image field inside a card or a deck item, and a video's poster. <code>0</code> keeps none: a replaced image is deleted, as before. Each kept image is the full original, so this uses real disk space. Gallery pictures go to the trash instead.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: keepFiles;"><label for="field-UID">Earlier Files per Field</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="keepFiles" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="0" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="0" min="0" max="50" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">How many replaced or removed files each <code>file</code> field of an object keeps, including a file field inside a card or a deck item. <code>0</code> keeps none. Each kept file is the full original: with large downloads, a small number here can use a lot of disk. Depot files go to the trash instead.</p></div><div class="form-field toggle-field " data-type="toggle" style="--grid-area: trash;"><label for="field-UID">Trash for Galleries and Depots</label><div class="form-group"><div class="switch"><input id="field-UID" name="trash" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="help-UID"/><label for="field-UID" aria-hidden="true">Trash for Galleries and Depots</label></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">Keep the pictures removed from a gallery and the files and folders removed from a depot, so restoring a snapshot brings them back. There is no count: everything removed is kept until it is older than Maximum Age, then deleted. Deleting a large depot therefore holds its disk space for that long.</p></div><div class="form-field number-field " data-type="number" style="--grid-area: maxFileSizeMB;"><label for="field-UID">Largest File Kept (MB)</label><div class="form-group"><input type="number" id="field-UID" name="maxFileSizeMB" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="100" aria-describedby="help-UID" value="100" min="0" max="102400" autocomplete="nofill"/><div class="form-group-icon"></div></div><p class="help" id="help-UID">A file larger than this is never kept, by any of the three settings above: it is deleted when it is replaced or removed, as before. Set to <code>0</code> for no limit.</p></div><div class="form-inline-fields"><button type="submit" class="button btn cms-save cms-button">Save Settings</button></div></form></div>